@startuml
title Recommended FHIR structure for HealthcareService scheduling characteristics

skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho

object "HealthcareService" as hs
object "characteristic[]\nCodeableConcept only" as characteristic
object "extension[]\nresource-level extensions" as extensions

object "CodeableConcept\ncode = scheduling-accepts-new" as acceptsNew
object "Coding\nsystem = wc-characteristic\ncode = scheduling-accepts-new" as acceptsNewCoding

object "CodeableConcept\ncode = scheduling-accepts-reschedule" as acceptsReschedule
object "Coding\nsystem = wc-characteristic\ncode = scheduling-accepts-reschedule" as acceptsRescheduleCoding

object "CodeableConcept\ncode = scheduling-accepts-cancellation" as acceptsCancellation
object "Coding\nsystem = wc-characteristic\ncode = scheduling-accepts-cancellation" as acceptsCancellationCoding

object "Extension\nurl = .../child-patient-threshold\nvalueInteger = clinic.childPatientThreshold" as childThreshold

hs --> characteristic
hs --> extensions

characteristic --> acceptsNew
acceptsNew --> acceptsNewCoding

characteristic --> acceptsReschedule
acceptsReschedule --> acceptsRescheduleCoding

characteristic --> acceptsCancellation
acceptsCancellation --> acceptsCancellationCoding

extensions --> childThreshold

note right of characteristic
Use characteristic for concepts that are
classifications or capabilities of the service.
Represent them as CodeableConcept with coding.
end note

note right of childThreshold
Use a dedicated extension for data that is
quantitative and not a coded service characteristic.
Prefer one named extension with valueInteger
over nested anonymous extension layers.
end note

note bottom of hs
FHIR best practice here:
- coded flags in characteristic[]
- custom numeric business rule in extension[]
- avoid mixing text-only characteristic entries
  with complex nested extensions
end note

@enduml